# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke and prefix job of this pack (the prefix gate serves the selection in its containers too and fails an arm whose log lacks the checkpoint lines), so each pair
# differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# A3 (OPTIONAL, the sliced restore under every audit): c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent-sliced on the audited twin
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit, no baseline: a session built to the largest size the profile admits, fresh-salt floods the size of the KV pool
# so it leaves the device pool for host RAM, SEVEN SEATS decoding, a 10 s settle and a 60 s control window, then the session RETURNS (restored from the host tier in slices
# of 512 blocks of at most 200 ms, the seats decoding between them), a long (120k) fresh prompt (SPILL), the returning turn's COLD TWIN. It runs on Swift (the prefix step
# forwards the selection). THE QUESTION: is a restore done in slices, at the 48 GiB tier, byte-identical to the whole one under every audit (verify=all, the read-back, the
# extent audit), beside the lone-user round? READ: the plan verdict PASS, every pair IDENTICAL, "host tier restore slice on blocks=512 ms=200" once, a restore line with
# slices above 1 and held_steps above 0, no slice over 1,000 ms, no "slice aborted" line the request's own end does not explain, no "fell back", zero failure counters, all
# seven seats across every judged window. A failure is NO-GO for the sliced-restore lines of the candidate (QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_RESTORE_SLICE and _MS in the ship entry of
# scripts/ci/fusion-wp/S5.json), not for the rest. OPT: an optional job the driver admits only if it fits the window. Estimate 100 minutes (the tier-slice pack's TS1).
# CHECKPOINT READ (the prefix gate checks every arm's container log; the smoke step passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the arm's result line says "checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a: read". RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other
# job beside it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent-sliced
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s5-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=180
